#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096653 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096452 :question/id #uuid "09d593cc-526e-5691-9a18-efff515eae59" :question/math-academy-id "e-4288" :question/problem "Consider the following diagram, where $\\overrightarrow{OA}=\\mathbf{a},$ $\\overrightarrow{OB}=\\mathbf{b},$ and $X$ divides $AB$ in the ratio $3:1.$ Find $\\overrightarrow{OX}.$\n\n![](images/67/678ea2936b8a5b1ded74cb8a0875c629e8be0f7002c98492ebf2e8109fc603ef.png)" :question/worked-solution "From the diagram, we see that\n\n$$\n\\overrightarrow{OX} = \\overrightarrow{OA}+\\overrightarrow{AX}.\n$$\n\nWe're told that $\\overrightarrow{OA} = \\mathbf{a},$ so we just need to work out $\\overrightarrow{AX}.$\n\nFirst, from $\\triangle OAB,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB} & =\\overset{\\to }{AO}+\\overset{\\to }{OB} \\\\  & =-\\overset{\\to }{OA}+\\overset{\\to }{OB} \\\\  & =-a+b \\\\  & =b-a.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $AX:XB=3:1,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\overrightarrow{AX}=\\dfrac{3}{4}\\overrightarrow{AB}=\\dfrac{3}{4}(\\mathbf{b}-\\mathbf{a}).\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{OX} & =\\overset{\\to }{OA}+\\overset{\\to }{AX} \\\\  & =a+\\frac{3}{4}(b-a) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}a+\\frac{3}{4}b.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "feae36e7-ae88-5f3a-957f-e65a92e399ad" :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186097046 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "95092ddd-a592-51a9-a935-ee8d21d09f58" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "OT^(→) = a + \\frac{1}{2}b" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186094250} {:answer/id #uuid "c8ea1899-3edc-5a44-a68d-8e0dc35e8f3e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "OT^(→) = \\frac{2}{3}a + \\frac{1}{3}b" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186094251} {:answer/id #uuid "0f332864-f317-5e8c-afc1-79039bba7d4b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "OT^(→) = \\frac{1}{3}a + \\frac{2}{3}b" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186094252