{csc}⁡x=2,$ then what is $\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{csc}⁡(x-4\\pi )+2?$" :question/worked-solution "The period of $y=\\operatorname{csc}⁡x$ is $2\\pi .$ Therefore, for integer $n$ we have\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{csc}⁡x=\\operatorname{csc}⁡(x+2n\\pi ).\n$$\n\nSubstituting $n=-2$ into the right-hand-side of the above gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{csc}⁡x=\\operatorname{csc}⁡(x+2\\cdot (-2)\\cdot \\pi )=\\operatorname{csc}⁡(x-4\\pi ).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, if $\\operatorname{csc}⁡x=2,$ then $\\operatorname{csc}⁡(x-4\\pi )=2.$\n\nFinally, then\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{csc}⁡(x-4\\pi )+2 & =\\frac{1}{4}(2)+2 \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}+2 \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186335892 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2116cd79-44ea-53c6-889d-f1682fbd66e6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186333285} {:answer/id #uuid "3d232036-8fad-5550-abc3-00107d785ebb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1+\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186333565} {:answer/id #uuid "71502cbf-4578-5c31-b861-904cd30b4751" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{5}+2\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334019} {:answer/id #uuid "78d38142-d9f0-58b7-a882-9c15bbb0ea41" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334072} {:answer/id #uuid "b85f9153-ad14-57e3-93d0-fc16c152374a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5\\sqrt{2}-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334605}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b85f9153-ad14-57e3-93d0-fc16c152374a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5\\sqrt{2}-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334605} :answer-field/id #uuid "48a2344e-da17-5c35-be6d-dd0a9ebe6076" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186335380}] :question/difficulty {:db/iden