"selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515840}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "898d4ab7-b593-5ece-8f08-6c24b9d07e0b" :question/problem "If $\\csc x = \\frac{7}{5}$, then what is $\\csc (x + 18π)$?" :question/worked-solution "The period of $y=\\operatorname{csc}⁡x$ is $2\\pi .$ Therefore, for integer $n$ we have\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{csc}⁡x=\\operatorname{csc}⁡(x+2n\\pi ).\n$$\n\nSubstituting $n=9$ into the right-hand-side of the above gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{csc}⁡x=\\operatorname{csc}⁡(x+2\\cdot 9\\cdot \\pi )=\\operatorname{csc}⁡(x+18\\pi ).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, if $\\operatorname{csc}⁡x=\\frac{7}{5},$ then $\\operatorname{csc}⁡(x+18\\pi )=\\frac{7}{5}.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186515831 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "859c7f1d-18e7-5145-9d69-668c6af915a8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "11" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515826} {:answer/id #uuid "8abce3c3-5843-5ae0-9faa-24cb3fbfbc52" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515828} {:answer/id #uuid "b176be31-65d5-52ae-9680-8ca870123db0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515833} {:answer/id #uuid "b9a1980d-86c4-53d3-9a07-f54bb81343dc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "16" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515834} {:answer/id #uuid "eb3b5083-7ece-5000-88ca-3033e5f0fe06" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515839}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "859c7f1d-18e7-5145-9d69-668c6af915a8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "11" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515826} :answer-field/id #uuid "c0aa6113-b532-5f98-abcc-5cd89dff376b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515835}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "af752b24-de14-5d01-9d2c-b286d82755be" :question/problem "If $\\operatorname{csc}⁡x=10,$ then what is $\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{csc}⁡(x+14\\pi )+6?$" :question/worked-solution "The period of $y=\\operatorname{csc}⁡x$ is $2\\pi .$ Therefore, for integer $n$ we have\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{csc}⁡x=\\operatorname{csc}⁡(x+2n\\pi ).\n$$\n\nSubstituting $n=7$ into the right-hand-side of the above gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{csc}⁡x=\\operatorname{csc}⁡(x+2\\cdot 7\\cdot \\pi )=\\operatorname{csc}⁡(x+14\\pi ).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, if $\\operatorname{csc}⁡x=10,$ then $\\operatorname{csc}⁡(x+14\\pi )=10.$\n\nFinally, then\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{csc}⁡(x+14\\pi )+6 & =\\frac{1}{2}(10)+6 \\\\  & =\\frac{10}{2}+6 \\\\  & =5+6 \\\\  & =11.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186515837 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1ff26c11-ebe2-5d50-b521-fce40d4c28f7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "36+144 \\pi" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515811} {:answer/id #uuid "7360afe5-b7c7-56c7-9c12-a07af7e493d4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515821} {:answer/id #uuid "7ae2a1a6-8b9b-58f8-be3b-6109ef998151" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "36" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515822} {:answer/id #uuid "b063966d-cb00-5ba1-aebb-6d105a5b8f8f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515832} {:answer/id #uuid "c1059fce-9b07-52a4-9821-dfa3066a79c5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515836}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7ae2a1a6-8b9b-58f8-be3b-6109ef998151" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "36" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515822} :answer-field/id #uuid "3da75829-6737-510a-b060-afd0291ac79f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515818}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "db02433d-d5bd-5e79-8d92-b83e2542bfdb" :question/problem "If $\\operatorname{csc}⁡x=6,$ then what is $6\\operatorname{csc}⁡(x+24\\pi )?$" :question/worked-solution "The period of $y=\\operatorname{csc}⁡x$ is $2\\pi .$ Therefore, for integer $n$ we have\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{csc}⁡x=\\operatorname{csc}⁡(x+2n\\pi ).\n$$\n\nSubstituting $n=12$ into the right-hand-side of the above gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{csc}⁡x=\\operatorname{csc}⁡(x+2\\cdot 12\\cdot \\pi )=\\operatorname{csc}⁡(x+24\\pi ).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, if $\\operatorname{csc}⁡x=6,$ then $\\operatorname{csc}⁡(x+24\\pi )=6.$\n\nFinally, then\n\n$$\n6\\operatorname{csc}⁡(x+24\\pi )=6\\cdot 6=36.\n$$"}] :knowledge-point/title "Utilizing the Periodicity Property of the Cosecant Function"}]}
